# Cursor AI Rules for DrillDraw Project

## Critical Rules

- **Plan before coding.** Create plan (objective, files, tests, ADRs) before implementation. See .cursor/rules/pr-flow.md.
- **Never work on main branch.** Always create a branch with an issue number first.
- **Pre-work:** Check branch (`git branch --show-current`). If on main, create branch `type/issue-number-description`, then start work.
- **Pre-commit:** Run `dart format .`, `flutter analyze`, `flutter test`, then commit. Fix all issues before committing.

## Documentation Map

Use these files for detailed rules. Cursor should read them when relevant:

- **Workflow**: .cursor/rules/workflow.md (branch, git, commit, troubleshooting)
- **Architecture**: .cursor/rules/architecture.md (shapes, selection, hit-test, canvas)
- **Decision trees**: .cursor/rules/decision-trees.md (when to do X, which docs to read)
- **PR and planning**: .cursor/rules/pr-flow.md (before coding, PR checklist)
- **Testing**: .cursor/rules/testing.md (when writing or reviewing tests)
- **Code quality**: .cursor/rules/code-quality.md (when writing/reviewing code)
- **Glossary**: .cursor/rules/glossary.md (terminology)
- **ADRs**: docs/ADR-*.md (architecture decisions)

## Memory Reminders

- Plan before coding; see pr-flow.md
- Never work on main; always use branch with issue number
- Pre-commit: format, analyze, test (see workflow.md)
- Applies to all work, including documentation
